  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The arithmetic mean of a set of observation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. If each observation is divided by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>,&nbsp;then the mean of the new series is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0Z8GX",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FaGmQ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Gh6Jl",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jGzqH",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> observations.</p><p>Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>&#931;</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Then. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>&#931;</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence option (c) is correct.</p>",
